00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:12.040
You can actually see the little turret move around in a circular motion, but it, it always

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:17.240
feels like they designed every enemy around like the worst possible spot for the metal

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:18.600
to shoot like that.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:24.020
Yeah. Everything is either like too low or like flies in a pattern that isn't great for the mech.

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:25.660
So you just are constantly missing.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:30.380
And this is a game where like, basically it doesn't pay to like stick around and fight

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:33.820
enemies. You just want to like kill what you can, but keep moving forward.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:39.600
I think it's there to incentivize like stomping because stomping is a valid way to destroy

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.940
enemies, but you can't walk over them and have a count as a stomp.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.420
Yeah. That's what I was going to say.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:48.380
I think that like the, it just encouraged me what for better or worse.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:53.100
It just, I like, it was way easier for me to just crush people than to try and, because

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.860
you also have to be in order to aim down.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:58.220
I mean, I feel like I, you have to be moving.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:01.220
So like you can't even really line yourself up and aim.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:02.220
You're always moving.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:06.600
And that makes it like impossible to actually like target anything.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:12.780
Technically you can be not moving and aim down, but you have to kind of move into it

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:22.300
first. It doesn't, it does not reset your turret position until I think either you press a, maybe select

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:27.940
or like, I think select is your like zero, like that's how you like your zero.

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:29.160
